column5:
Meet us at The Bean to change Sen. Durbin’s mind and urge him to fight for voting rights, care jobs, and a green climate! This event is family friendly and includes art, umbrellas with Senator Durbin's image, leafletting, and a short march.

Senator Durbin HAS NOT COMMITTED to standing up to corporations, the 1% and their rich friends in the Senate who are blocking voting rights, shielding themselves from paying taxes, watering down President Biden's historic Jobs and Families Plans, and preventing a transition to renewable energy. 

Durbin's legacy is at stake. We need him to deliver for our families, no excuses! Time is running out for the Senate to:
- Expand voting rights, get money out of politics and end gerrymandering;
- Create paid family leave;
- Make monthly cash payments for low-income families with children permanent;
- Invest hundreds of billions in childcare and home health care, clean water, and affordable housing;
- Transition us to green energy and ensure communities of color and people who currently work in fossil fuels can get millions of new jobs.

@aoc nails it: We don't have a second more to waste when it comes to the climate crisis. Our future is on the line right now. 🌎

Climate change is the single-greatest threat to humanity and the existential battle of our time. Only by standing together and demanding change can we win this fight. ✊

#AOC #ClimateCrisis #ClimateChange #Climate #ClimateEmergency #GlobalWarming #BuildBackBetter #BuildBackBetterAct #PlanetEarth #Environment #COP26 #LCV #Quotes.
